<title>USA: Hottest entrepreneurial areas in U.S..</title>
<headline>Hottest entrepreneurial areas in U.S..</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a list of the top 10 states and large and small metropolitan areas where start-up companies are finding the most success, according to Cognetics Inc.</p>
<p>STATES</p>
<p>1. Utah</p>
<p>2. Arizona</p>
<p>3. Nevada</p>
<p>4. Alabama</p>
<p>5. Virgina</p>
<p>6. Georgia</p>
<p>7. Colorado</p>
<p>8. Tennessee</p>
<p>9. Florida</p>
<p>10. New Mexico</p>
<p>LARGE METROPOLITAN AREAS</p>
<p>1. Salt Lake City-Provo</p>
<p>2. Atlanta</p>
<p>3. Birmingham-Tuscaloosa, Ala.</p>
<p>4. Phoenix</p>
<p>5. Washington, DC</p>
<p>6. Orlando, Fla.</p>
<p>7. Raleigh-Durham, N.C.</p>
<p>8. Minneapolis-St. Paul</p>
<p>9. Indianapolis</p>
<p>10. Nashville, Tenn.</p>
<p>SMALLER METROPOLITAN AREAS</p>
<p>1. Las Vegas</p>
<p>2. Huntsville, Ala.</p>
<p>3. Austin, Texas</p>
<p>4. Boise, Idaho</p>
<p>5. Albuquerque, N.M.</p>
<p>6. Sioux Falls, S.D.</p>
<p>7. Tucson, Ariz.</p>
<p>8. Pensacola, Fla.</p>
<p>9. Lincoln, Neb.</p>
<p>10. Springfiled, Mo.</p>
